From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mathieu GRENET <mathieu@mgth.fr>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 17:35:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/28] ad_orender: load liborender at runtime with an ABI
 handshake

mpv linked liborender at build time (DT_NEEDED liborender.so.0), which
welded every release to the engine version it was built against and gave
Windows (no soname) no protection at all against a mismatched DLL.

Load it with dlopen instead, through a function table resolved once per
process (common/orender_dl.[ch]) against the vendored ABI header
common/orender_abi.h (generated by cbindgen in the Omniphony repo, ABI
0.5). Search order:

  1. --ad-orender-library=PATH   (new option; failure is final)
  2.             (same hard-fail semantics)
  3. the Studio-deployed per-user library
     (~/.local/share/omniphony/lib, ~/Library/Application Support/...,
     %LOCALAPPDATA%\omniphony\lib)
  4. next to the mpv executable  (the lib bundled in release zips)
  5. the bare soname via the system loader (not on Windows, where a
     relative mp_dlopen resolves against the CWD)

A candidate must export the version handshake and report the ABI major
mpv was compiled against; required symbols are batch-resolved, optional
ones (overlay group, set_option, build_id) fall back to no-op stubs so
call sites stay unconditional and both skew directions degrade
gracefully. Rejected candidates fall through to the next location, so a
stale Studio deployment degrades to the bundled fallback instead of
killing spatial audio. Load failure routes the decoder into the existing
force_host native-decode path with one actionable warning; the overlay
quietly does not start.

Also replaces the hand-maintained OR_* channel-label mirror enum with
OrenderChannelLabel from the vendored header (the Omniphony side now
exports it, tested against the engine's enum), moves the option struct
to ad_orender.h (the loader needs the library path before any decoder
exists), and drops the pkg-config dependency: the orender feature is now
source-only, so mpv builds with no Omniphony checkout at all.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
